<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk.Razor">

  <!--
    MAUI Blazor Hybrid app for iOS and Android (plus macOS and Windows for desktop testing).
    Hosts the shared TvTracker.UI components and talks to the services only through the Mobile BFF.
    Signs in with Keycloak in the system browser (OIDC + PKCE), keeps tokens in secure storage,
    caches data and queues changes in SQLite for offline use, and handles tvtracker:// deep links.
    Not part of the AppHost: run it from Visual Studio / VS Code / Rider while the AppHost is running.
  -->

  <PropertyGroup>
    <!-- Directory.Build.props sets a single TargetFramework; clear it so this project can multi-target. -->
    <TargetFramework></TargetFramework>
    <!-- iOS and Mac Catalyst build only on a Mac (their workload doesn't exist for Linux), so a Linux build, such as CI,
         targets Android alone. -->
    <TargetFrameworks Condition="!$([MSBuild]::IsOSPlatform('linux'))">net10.0-android;net10.0-ios;net10.0-maccatalyst</TargetFrameworks>
    <TargetFrameworks Condition="$([MSBuild]::IsOSPlatform('linux'))">net10.0-android</TargetFrameworks>
    <TargetFrameworks Condition="$([MSBuild]::IsOSPlatform('windows'))">$(TargetFrameworks);net10.0-windows10.0.19041.0</TargetFrameworks>

    <OutputType>Exe</OutputType>
    <RootNamespace>TvTracker.Mobile</RootNamespace>
    <UseMaui>true</UseMaui>
    <SingleProject>true</SingleProject>
    <EnableDefaultCssItems>false</EnableDefaultCssItems>

    <!-- MAUI packages follow the MAUI workload version, so this project doesn't use central package versions. -->
    <ManagePackageVersionsCentrally>false</ManagePackageVersionsCentrally>

    <ApplicationTitle>TV Tracker</ApplicationTitle>
    <ApplicationId>com.tvtracker.mobile</ApplicationId>
    <!-- The version people see, and the build number the stores order uploads by: each upload needs a higher
         ApplicationVersion than the last. A release passes both (-p:ApplicationDisplayVersion=1.2 -p:ApplicationVersion=17). -->
    <ApplicationDisplayVersion Condition="'$(ApplicationDisplayVersion)' == ''">1.0</ApplicationDisplayVersion>
    <ApplicationVersion Condition="'$(ApplicationVersion)' == ''">1</ApplicationVersion>

    <!-- Where the app finds the backend. Empty, it is a development build that talks to the AppHost on this machine.
         A release names the deployment's host (PUBLIC_HOST in scripts/deploy.sh): -p:TvTrackerPublicHost=tv.example.com.
         TvTrackerApiAddress overrides the gateway's address where the deployment gives it its own host (API_HOST). -->
    <TvTrackerPublicHost Condition="'$(TvTrackerPublicHost)' == ''"></TvTrackerPublicHost>
    <TvTrackerApiAddress Condition="'$(TvTrackerApiAddress)' == ''"></TvTrackerApiAddress>
    <!-- The backend's Catalog:Provider (tvmaze, wikidata, tvdb), for the credit its licence requires. -->
    <TvTrackerCatalogSource Condition="'$(TvTrackerCatalogSource)' == ''">tvmaze</TvTrackerCatalogSource>

    <!-- Run as an unpackaged app on Windows -->
    <WindowsPackageType>None</WindowsPackageType>

    <SupportedOSPlatformVersion Condition="$([MSBuild]::GetTargetPlatformIdentifier('$(TargetFramework)')) == 'ios'">15.0</SupportedOSPlatformVersion>
    <SupportedOSPlatformVersion Condition="$([MSBuild]::GetTargetPlatformIdentifier('$(TargetFramework)')) == 'maccatalyst'">15.0</SupportedOSPlatformVersion>
    <SupportedOSPlatformVersion Condition="$([MSBuild]::GetTargetPlatformIdentifier('$(TargetFramework)')) == 'android'">24.0</SupportedOSPlatformVersion>
    <SupportedOSPlatformVersion Condition="$([MSBuild]::GetTargetPlatformIdentifier('$(TargetFramework)')) == 'windows'">10.0.17763.0</SupportedOSPlatformVersion>
    <TargetPlatformMinVersion Condition="$([MSBuild]::GetTargetPlatformIdentifier('$(TargetFramework)')) == 'windows'">10.0.17763.0</TargetPlatformMinVersion>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!-- A release for the store: an app bundle, which is what Google Play takes, with R8 shrinking the Java side as Play
       asks. Signed when a keystore is named (-p:AndroidSigningKeyStore=...), which sets AndroidKeyStore; the passwords
       come from files (file:...), never from this project. See README, Releasing the Android app. -->
  <PropertyGroup Condition="$([MSBuild]::GetTargetPlatformIdentifier('$(TargetFramework)')) == 'android' and '$(Configuration)' == 'Release'">
    <AndroidPackageFormats>aab</AndroidPackageFormats>
    <AndroidLinkTool>r8</AndroidLinkTool>
    <AndroidR8ObfuscationMode>private-members</AndroidR8ObfuscationMode>
    <AndroidKeyStore Condition="'$(AndroidSigningKeyStore)' != ''">true</AndroidKeyStore>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!-- MobileSettings reads these back at run time. -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <AssemblyMetadata Include="TvTracker.PublicHost" Value="$(TvTrackerPublicHost)" />
    <AssemblyMetadata Include="TvTracker.ApiAddress" Value="$(TvTrackerApiAddress)" />
    <AssemblyMetadata Include="TvTracker.CatalogSource" Value="$(TvTrackerCatalogSource)" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!-- A release that talks to this machine would be useless on anyone's phone, and it would do so over plain http. -->
  <Target Name="RequirePublicHostForRelease" BeforeTargets="CoreCompile" Condition="'$(Configuration)' == 'Release' and '$(TvTrackerPublicHost)' == '' and '$(TvTrackerAllowLocalRelease)' != 'true'">
    <Error Text="A Release build needs the deployment's host: -p:TvTrackerPublicHost=tv.example.com (README, Releasing the Android app). To build a Release against this machine for testing, pass -p:TvTrackerAllowLocalRelease=true." />
  </Target>

  <ItemGroup>
    <MauiIcon Include="Resources\AppIcon\appicon.svg" ForegroundFile="Resources\AppIcon\appiconfg.svg" Color="#1C1917" />
    <MauiSplashScreen Include="Resources\Splash\splash.svg" Color="#1C1917" BaseSize="128,128" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Maui.Controls" Version="$(MauiVersion)" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.WebView.Maui" Version="$(MauiVersion)" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Logging.Debug" Version="$(RuntimeVersion)" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Http" Version="$(RuntimeVersion)" />
    <PackageReference Include="IdentityModel.OidcClient" Version="6.0.0" />
    <!-- Feature flags: OpenFeature over OFREP, through the BFF's /features route (the services use flagd's own provider). -->
    <PackageReference Include="OpenFeature.Hosting" Version="2.14.1" />
    <PackageReference Include="OpenFeature.Providers.Ofrep" Version="0.1.7" />
    <PackageReference Include="sqlite-net-pcl" Version="1.11.285" />
    <PackageReference Include="SQLitePCLRaw.bundle_green" Version="2.1.11" />
    <!-- bundle_green 2.1.11 brings in lib.e_sqlite3 2.1.11, which has a known high-severity vulnerability (GHSA-2m69-gcr7-jv3q). -->
    <PackageReference Include="SQLitePCLRaw.lib.e_sqlite3" Version="2.1.14" Condition="$([MSBuild]::GetTargetPlatformIdentifier('$(TargetFramework)')) != 'android'" />
    <!-- On Android the e_sqlite3 pins only keep the audit clean. They ship no binaries: SourceGear.sqlite3 (via sqlite-net-pcl) is the single native SQLite, and a second libe_sqlite3.so (glibc or Android) collides with it in the APK. -->
    <PackageReference Include="SQLitePCLRaw.lib.e_sqlite3" Version="2.1.14" ExcludeAssets="runtime;native;contentFiles" Condition="$([MSBuild]::GetTargetPlatformIdentifier('$(TargetFramework)')) == 'android'" />
    <PackageReference Include="SQLitePCLRaw.lib.e_sqlite3.android" Version="2.1.14" ExcludeAssets="all" Condition="$([MSBuild]::GetTargetPlatformIdentifier('$(TargetFramework)')) == 'android'" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\TvTracker.UI\TvTracker.UI.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
